# clonal escape — why a mutation you got as a child becomes a disease at sixty
#
# `erythropoiesis-pv.strombild` models POLYCYTHEMIA VERA AS AN END STATE: one edge
# already rewired, a marrow that already ignores EPO. It is right about the steady
# state and silent about the forty years before it, which is the part that makes the
# disease strange. THIS FILE MODELS THOSE FORTY YEARS.
#
# THE PUZZLE. PV is "genetic" — a point mutation, JAK2 V617F. So you would expect
# children with too many red cells. You do not get that. Median age at diagnosis is
# about sixty. Meanwhile most people who carry a low-level V617F clone never develop
# PV at all. A germline defect does not behave like this: when the broken gene is in
# every cell from conception, the disease arrives in childhood — which is exactly what
# familial erythrocytosis (Schaltwerk's `pfcp`, a truncated EPO receptor) does.
#
# THE RESOLUTION, AND THE HYPOTHESIS THIS FILE MAKES RUNNABLE. V617F is SOMATIC: it
# happens in ONE blood stem cell, in one person, during their life. Lineage-tracing
# work published in 2022 dated that event to childhood or before birth in the patients
# studied — so the mutation often IS early. What takes decades is the CLONE. One cell
# with a small self-renewal advantage has to grow into a large fraction of the marrow
# before the blood count moves.
#
#     the disease is not the mutation.
#     the disease is the mutation x the share of your marrow descended from it x time.
#
# A share and a rate: stock and flow. So the natural history is the model.
#
# THE DIAL IS THE `k` ON THE NICHE EDGE. It is how much faster the mutant stem cell
# renews than its wild-type neighbours, and it competes against `drift`, the rate at
# which a small clone loses its share again. With a niche of 100, a small clone's net
# growth rate is `100k - drift` per year, so the escape condition is just `100k > drift`.
#
# TURN ONLY THAT NUMBER AND THE WHOLE NATURAL HISTORY MOVES. Everything below is the
# model's own output, mutation fixed at age 10, nothing else touched:
#
#     k        net/yr   clone at 85    hematocrit    blood count    meets PV
#                          (% niche)       at 85       looks odd     criteria
#     0.0004   -0.01         0.0           45.0          never        never
#     0.0008   +0.03         0.1           45.0          never        never
#     0.0012   +0.07         1.8           45.2          never        never
#     0.0018   +0.13        50.6           53.2         age 74       age 83
#     0.0024   +0.19        78.8           63.9         age 54       age 60
#     0.0035   +0.30        85.7           67.5         age 38       age 41
#     0.0050   +0.45        90.0           69.8         age 29       age 31
#
# THERE ARE THREE OUTCOMES, NOT TWO, AND THE MIDDLE ONE IS THE INTERESTING ONE.
#   * NO ESCAPE (k below 0.0005). The clone never gets going. Nothing to find.
#   * ESCAPE WITHOUT DISEASE (k around 0.0008 to 0.0012). The clone is real, growing,
#     and detectable by a sensitive assay — and the blood count is normal for life.
#     THIS IS CLONAL HEMATOPOIESIS, and it is most of the people who carry V617F. The
#     model did not need a second mechanism to produce them. Same mutation, same
#     physiology, a slightly smaller advantage, and the disease simply runs out of
#     lifetime. That is the file's main claim.
#   * DISEASE (k above about 0.0018). The clone crosses into a moving blood count, and
#     the age at which it does is set by the dial.
#
# THE SHIPPED VALUE, k = 0.0024, PUTS THE PV CRITERIA AT AGE 60. The median age at
# diagnosis of polycythemia vera is about sixty. That was not fitted to it — it is
# where a plausible growth rate lands, and it is the one number here worth taking
# seriously as a prediction. AGE OF ONSET IS AN OUTPUT IN THIS FILE, NOT A SETTING.
#
# AND THE SENSITIVITY IS THE WARNING. Doubling the dial from 0.0018 to 0.0035 moves
# first abnormality from age 74 to age 38. A model this steep cannot predict an
# individual's onset from a loosely-estimated advantage, and saying so is the point:
# it tells you how well that number would have to be measured to be worth anything.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE DOES NOT CLAIM.
#   * The niche edge is BOOKKEEPING FOR COMPETITION, not a conversion. Mutant cells do
#     not turn neighbours mutant; they out-renew them for a fixed number of niche
#     slots, and `normal_hsc -> mutant_hsc` is how a fixed-total displacement is
#     written with stocks. The logistic shape is the claim; the arrow's direction of
#     travel is an accounting choice.
#   * CLONE EXPANSION IS DETERMINISTIC HERE AND IS A STOCHASTIC PROCESS IN A PERSON.
#     A clone's early life is a handful of cells, where chance dominates and `drift`
#     is a smooth stand-in for a coin flip. So this file can say WHETHER a given
#     advantage escapes on average. It cannot give the probability that it does, and
#     the real answer to "why do most carriers never get PV" may be mostly that
#     probability. See `holes` on Nordstern's `polycythaemia-vera`.
#   * The mutant fraction of progenitors is taken to EQUAL the stem-cell clone
#     fraction. Declared, not derived.
#   * TIME IS IN YEARS, so EPO and the progenitor pool are run far slower than life.
#     Real EPO has a half-life of about five hours and these constants equilibrate it
#     in weeks. On a decade scale that is still instantaneous, so the slow curves are
#     right and anything inside a month in this file is not.
#   * No treatment. This is the untreated natural history on purpose — the whole point
#     is the age the line is crossed. `erythropoiesis-pv.strombild` has the phlebotomy.
#
# THE MISSING DATA, STATED. To predict a real person's age of onset you would need
# their advantage, and nobody measures it. What is measurable is allele burden at two
# timepoints, which gives the growth rate directly. That measurement, in carriers
# rather than patients, is the experiment this model is asking for.

node age         : range(0, 90),  init(0)  @ box(fill = squares)                    # years lived
node normal_hsc  : range(0, 100), init(100) @ bucket(fill = dots)                   # wild-type stem cells, % of niche
node mutant_hsc  : range(0, 100), init(0)  @ bucket(fill = squares)                 # the V617F clone, % of niche
node epo         : range(0, 120), init(10) @ bucket(fill = water)                   # plasma erythropoietin, mU/mL
node progenitors : range(0, 200), init(50) @ bucket(fill = dots)                    # erythroid precursors
node red_cells   : range(0, 80),  init(45) @ bucket(fill = water, threshold = 48)   # red-cell mass as hematocrit, %

node mutated     : range(0, 1), init(0) @ box     # latches when the mutation happens
node noticed     : range(0, 1), init(0) @ box     # latches at a hematocrit a blood count would flag
node diagnosable : range(0, 1), init(0) @ box     # latches at a hematocrit that meets the PV threshold
node clot_zone   : range(0, 1), init(0) @ box     # latches where viscosity drives thrombotic risk

external lifetime     # the clock
external kidney
external clearance
external marrow
external apoptosis
external spleen

lifetime    -> age         : constant(c = 1)                                            # one year per year

# THE CLONE. logistic displacement in a fixed niche, against loss by drift.
normal_hsc  -> mutant_hsc  : product(of = normal_hsc, by = mutant_hsc, k = 0.0024)      # <<< THE DIAL
mutant_hsc  -> normal_hsc  : proportional(of = mutant_hsc, k = 0.05)                    # drift

# THE LOOP, unchanged in structure from `erythropoiesis.strombild`.
kidney      -> epo         : repress(of = red_cells, max = 1700, k = 35, n = 8)         # the sensor is fine
epo         -> clearance   : proportional(of = epo, k = 20)
marrow      -> progenitors : constant(c = 1137)
progenitors -> apoptosis   : proportional(of = progenitors, k = 20)

# TWO MATURATION EDGES, AND THE CLONE SETS THE SECOND ONE'S WEIGHT.
# wild-type precursors mature only with EPO. V617F precursors signal as though EPO
# were bound when it is not, so their edge reads the clone and ignores the hormone.
progenitors -> red_cells   : product(of = progenitors, by = epo, k = 0.274)             # EPO-dependent
progenitors -> red_cells   : product(of = progenitors, by = mutant_hsc, k = 0.050)      # EPO-independent

red_cells   -> spleen      : proportional(of = red_cells, k = 3.04)                     # 120-day lifespan

event mutation    : age >= 10 & mutated == 0     : mutated = 1, mutant_hsc += 0.01, normal_hsc -= 0.01
event notice      : red_cells >= 48 & noticed == 0     : noticed = 1
event meets_criteria : red_cells >= 52 & diagnosable == 0 : diagnosable = 1
event thrombotic  : red_cells >= 55 & clot_zone == 0   : clot_zone = 1

pathway clone : normal_hsc->mutant_hsc, mutant_hsc->normal_hsc
pathway blood : kidney->epo, epo->clearance, marrow->progenitors, progenitors->apoptosis, red_cells->spleen
